        "type": "the-purpose",
        "title": "Untitled",
        "body": "This topic set provides a strategic foundation in the physics governing black holes and their surrounding environments. The topics focus on the core theoretical concepts necessary to understand how these extreme objects function and interact with the cosmos. Covered principles include the **defining physics of the event horizon**, the **fundamental conservation laws** that govern how BHs spin and grow, the **physical structure of the accretion disk** that fuels them, and the **unified model** that explains the diverse observational manifestations of Active Galactic Nuclei (AGN). Mastery of these principles is crucial for engaging with more advanced topics like gravitational waves, jet formation, and galaxy co-evolution.",
        "line_number": 33,
